  "preamble": "Spirantization of the palatalized velar [ɡʲ] to the postalveolar fricative [ʒ] moves the closure forward and releases it as friction. In Berber, the Proto-Berber palatalized velar *gʲ (written *ǵ in Wiktionary and *ɟ by some authors) became ʒ in the Zenati languages of Morocco and Algeria, including Riffian, Chenoua and the Mzab–Wargla group with Figuig, while most other Berber languages merged it with plain g, so that Riffian ajdir 'cliff, slope' and jen 'to sleep' answer to Kabyle agadir and gen.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Spirantization, Palatalization",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Riffian (Tarifit)",
      "languageFamily": "Zenati",
      "examples": [
